==English==

===Etymology===
Middle English statly, from state, state, rank; see  [[state]].
You know its kinda like dignified, like someone (e.g. a diplomat, ambassador or king) representing a state and that....

===Adverb===
'''stately'''

# In a [[regal]] manner; worthy of respect.

===Usage notes===
If someone has an English accent that is understated and not too [[wanker|wankerish]] it could be regarded as stately.

